This app uses lennoxapi 0.1.2 by Luke Alonso, declared MIT in its package
metadata and README: https://github.com/lukealonso/lennoxapi
Published source revision: e9e04d5d23e8253fd55132ef4bbf236f232d565a.

Its public classes parse the Lennox LAN protocol. This app supplies a bounded
HTTP transport, local sender routing, a separate partial command builder, and
the Homey integration. Homebridge-specific implementation files are not copied.

The upstream published archive does not include a standalone LICENSE file;
its declared license is recorded here without inventing an upstream notice.
The dependency and its package metadata are included in the installed bundle.

Controller identity feature mappings follow the protocol behavior in Pete
Rager's original Python client: https://github.com/PeteRager/lennoxs30api
The identity decoder is independently implemented here; no live identifiers or
upstream fixture files are included.

